511:  
512: -   The seven state tokens, one per weather state in canonical order:
513: -
514: -     wx-clear     #56B4E9   sky blue (Okabe-Ito), calm and no shortfall
515: -     wx-cloudy    #46617c   cloud slate, long runway with a spending gap
516: -     wx-overcast  #2f4257   deep slate, the darker sibling of cloudy
517: -     wx-rain      #2f7f7c   water lit, spending driven 3.0 to 11.9 months
518: -     wx-drought   #d97b3f   drought orange, income covers 65 percent or less
519: -     wx-storm     #ff6a4d   storm vermillion, runway under 3.0 months
520: -     wx-flood     #10333f   water deep, buffer depleted or runway at 0.0
521: +   Band vocabulary (src/lib/verdict.ts owns every band): the five verdict
522: +   bands, Critical, Storm warning, Watch, Fair skies, and Clear, carry all
523: +   color on these surfaces through their tailwind cp class and
524: +   currentColor, so the badge and the strip share one source of band
525: +   color (see the .wx-slot rule below). The seven state ladder from the
526: +   E3 draft left with weatherState.ts, and its unused palette tokens were
527: +   deleted with it.
528: +
529: +   The one state accent kept is wx-storm #ff6a4d, storm vermillion, used
530: +   only as a marker: the worst case continuation, the EI cliff line, and
531: +   the storm tag. It never sets a band.
532:  
533:     Plus the two grounds every surface sits on: wx-grounds #070c18 (the
534:     archival navy, same value as --rp-void but read from its own token so
535:     this file never depends on --rp-) and wx-parchment #e9e0c9 for text.
536: -
537: -   Soft tints (each state color at 26 percent over wx-grounds) carry every
538: -   printed label, so measured contrast for parchment text stays above
539: -   WCAG AA on all seven cells (worst case 9.3 to 1 on wx-clear-soft).
540: -   Solid state colors are used for tile fills, swatches, and rules only,
